## Why a log bucket at all?

You don't need a new bucket to store logs in Cloud Logging. The agent already sends logs there, into the project's `_Default` bucket. A log bucket is Cloud Logging's own storage, not a Cloud Storage bucket. Create `cn-staging-logs-me2` only for the location rule.

| Your goal | Needs a new bucket? |
|---|---|
| Logs survive a server being deleted | No |
| Keep them 180 days | No, raise `_Default` retention from 90 |
| Store them in `me-central2` | **Yes**, because a bucket's location can't be changed |

If compliance accepts global storage for logs, raise `_Default` to 180 days and skip the new bucket. Which one applies?

